/-!
# Finite SAGBI bases of permutation-invariant polynomial algebras

Let `G ≤ Equiv.Perm σ` be a permutation group acting on `MvPolynomial σ R` by variable renaming
(in the given permutation coordinates), and let `m : MonomialOrder σ` be any monomial order. This
file proves the Reichstein / Thiéry–Thomassé characterization: `permInvariantSubalgebra G R` has a
finite `m`-SAGBI basis if and only if `G` is generated by transpositions, equivalently `G` is the
direct product of the full symmetric groups on its orbits
(`TauCeti.fiberSubgroup (Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ))`).

* **Positive direction** (over an arbitrary commutative semiring `R`): when `G` is generated by
  transpositions, every `m`-maximal orbit exponent is weakly decreasing along each `G`-orbit
  ordered by `m`. Telescoping along each orbit expresses every leading exponent as a nonnegative
  integer combination of the leading exponents of the elementary symmetric polynomials in the
  individual `G`-orbits (`MvPolynomial.blockEsymm`), which are monic and form a finite `m`-SAGBI
  basis (`MonomialOrder.isSAGBIBasis_blockEsymmSet`).
* **Negative direction** (over any nontrivial commutative semiring without zero divisors, hence
  every field in every characteristic): a finite `m`-SAGBI basis forces the monoid
  `m.maxOrbitExponents G` of `m`-maximal orbit exponents to be finitely generated. Embedding into
  `σ → ℚ`, the generated rational pointed cone `C` is polyhedral by Minkowski–Weyl duality
  (`PointedCone.fg_iff_dualFG`), and its `G`-translates cover the nonnegative orthant with disjoint
  interiors. Walking along a generic rational segment from a point in `C` to a perturbation of its
  `g`-translate crosses the bounding hyperplanes and coordinate-equality hyperplanes one at a time,
  factoring `g` into transpositions in `G`.

## Main definitions

* `MonomialOrder.maxOrbitExponents`: the additive submonoid of `m`-maximal orbit exponents.
* `MvPolynomial.blockEsymm`: the `j`-th elementary symmetric polynomial in the variables of a
  single `G`-orbit.
* `MvPolynomial.blockEsymmSet`: the finite set of nontrivial block elementary symmetric polynomials.

## Main results

* `MonomialOrder.isSAGBIBasis_blockEsymmSet`: if `G` is generated by transpositions, the block
  elementary symmetric polynomials form a finite `m`-SAGBI basis over any commutative semiring `R`.
* `MonomialOrder.fg_maxOrbitExponents_iff_closure_isSwap_eq`: `m.maxOrbitExponents G` is finitely
  generated if and only if `G` is generated by transpositions.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff`: over any nontrivial
  commutative semiring without zero divisors, `permInvariantSubalgebra G R` admits a finite
  `m`-SAGBI basis if and only if `G` is generated by transpositions.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff_eq_fiberSubgroup`:
  equivalently, if and only if `G = TauCeti.fiberSubgroup (Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ))`.

## References

* L. Robbiano, M. Sweedler, *Subalgebra bases*, in *Commutative Algebra (Salvador, 1988)*,
  Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1430, Springer, 1990, 61–87.
* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 11.
* M. Göbel, *A constructive description of SAGBI bases for polynomial invariants of permutation
  groups*, J. Symbolic Comput. **26** (1998).
* N. M. Thiéry, S. Thomassé, *Convex cones and SAGBI bases of permutation invariants*, in
  *Invariant Theory in All Characteristics*, CRM Proc. Lecture Notes 35, AMS, 2004.
-/

public section

open Equiv

/-! ### The monoid of `m`-maximal orbit exponents -/

namespace MonomialOrder

open MvPolynomial

variable {σ R : Type*}

/-- The additive submonoid of exponent vectors `d : σ →₀ ℕ` that are `m`-maximal in their
`G`-orbit. -/
def maxOrbitExponents (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) : AddSubmonoid (σ →₀ ℕ) where
  carrier := {d | ∀ g ∈ G, d.equivMapDomain g ≼[m] d}
  zero_mem' g _ := by simp
  add_mem' {a b} ha hb g hg := by
    have hadd : (a + b).equivMapDomain g = a.equivMapDomain g + b.equivMapDomain g := by
      simp [Finsupp.equivMapDomain_eq_mapDomain, Finsupp.mapDomain_add]
    rw [hadd, map_add, map_add]
    exact add_le_add (ha g hg) (hb g hg)

@[simp]
theorem mem_maxOrbitExponents_iff (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (d : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G ↔ ∀ g ∈ G, d.equivMapDomain g ≼[m] d :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The leading-exponent monoid of `permInvariantSubalgebra G R` is `m.maxOrbitExponents G`. -/
theorem leadingExponents_permInvariantSubalgebra_eq (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) [Finite G] (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [NoZeroDivisors R]
    [Nontrivial R] :
    m.leadingExponents (permInvariantSubalgebra G R) = m.maxOrbitExponents G := by
  ext d
  exact m.mem_leadingExponents_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff

/-- Over any commutative semiring, every element of `Algebra.adjoin R (m.leadingTerm '' B)` is
supported in `AddSubmonoid.closure (m.degree '' (B \ {0}))`. -/
private theorem support_subset_closure_degree_of_mem_adjoin_leadingTerm (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    [CommSemiring R] {B : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)} {p : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hp : p ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (m.leadingTerm '' B)) :
    (p.support : Set (σ →₀ ℕ)) ⊆ AddSubmonoid.closure (m.degree '' (B \ {0})) := by
  classical
  induction hp using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem _ hx =>
    obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hx
    rcases eq_or_ne b 0 with rfl | hb0
    · simp
    · intro e he
      have hsup : (m.leadingTerm b).support ⊆ {m.degree b} := by
        rw [leadingTerm]
        exact support_monomial_subset
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp (hsup he)]
      exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure ⟨b, ⟨hb, hb0⟩, rfl⟩
  | algebraMap c =>
    intro e he
    have hsup : (C c : MvPolynomial σ R).support ⊆ {0} := by
      rw [← monomial_zero']
      exact support_monomial_subset
    rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp (hsup he)]
    exact zero_mem _
  | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
    refine (Finset.coe_subset.2 support_add).trans ?_
    rw [Finset.coe_union]
    exact Set.union_subset hx hy
  | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
    refine (Finset.coe_subset.2 (support_mul x y)).trans ?_
    rw [Finset.coe_add]
    exact Set.add_subset_iff.2 fun a ha b hb => add_mem (hx ha) (hy hb)

/-- If a subalgebra `A` over a nontrivial commutative semiring without zero divisors has a finite
`m`-SAGBI basis, then its monoid of leading exponents `m.leadingExponents A` is finitely
generated. -/
theorem fg_leadingExponents_of_finite_isSAGBIBasis (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    [CommSemiring R] [NoZeroDivisors R] [Nontrivial R]
    {B : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)} {A : Subalgebra R (MvPolynomial σ R)}
    (hBfin : B.Finite) (hB : m.IsSAGBIBasis B A) :
    (m.leadingExponents A).FG := by
  rw [AddSubmonoid.fg_iff]
  refine ⟨m.degree '' (B \ {0}), le_antisymm ?_ ?_, (hBfin.subset Set.sdiff_subset).image m.degree⟩
  · rw [AddSubmonoid.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨b, ⟨hb, hb0⟩, rfl⟩
    exact m.degree_mem_leadingExponents (hB.subset hb) hb0
  · intro d hd
    rw [mem_leadingExponents_iff] at hd
    obtain ⟨f, hfA, hf0, rfl⟩ := hd
    have hlt : m.leadingTerm f ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (m.leadingTerm '' B) := by
      rw [hB.adjoin_leadingTerm]
      exact m.leadingTerm_mem_initialAlgebra hfA
    have hmem : m.degree f ∈ (m.leadingTerm f).support := by
      classical
      rw [mem_support_iff, leadingTerm, coeff_monomial]
      simpa using m.leadingCoeff_ne_zero_iff.mpr hf0
    exact m.support_subset_closure_degree_of_mem_adjoin_leadingTerm hlt hmem

end MonomialOrder

/-! ### Block elementary symmetric polynomials and the positive SAGBI direction -/

namespace MvPolynomial

variable {σ R : Type*}

/-- The `j`-th elementary symmetric polynomial in the variables belonging to a single `G`-orbit
`o`. -/
noncomputable def blockEsymm [Finite σ] (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R]
    (o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) (j : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ R :=
  letI : Fintype {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} := Fintype.ofFinite _
  rename Subtype.val (esymm {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} R j)

/-- A block elementary symmetric polynomial is invariant under `G`. -/
theorem blockEsymm_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra [Finite σ] (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    [CommSemiring R] (o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) (j : ℕ) :
    blockEsymm G R o j ∈ permInvariantSubalgebra G R := by
  rw [mem_permInvariantSubalgebra]
  intro g hg
  let _ : Fintype {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} := Fintype.ofFinite _
  have hfib : ∀ i : σ, Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) (g i) =
      Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i :=
    TauCeti.mem_fiberSubgroup.mp (TauCeti.le_fiberSubgroup_orbitRel G hg)
  let go : Perm {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} :=
    g.subtypePerm fun i => by rw [hfib i]
  have hcomp : (⇑g ∘ (Subtype.val : {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} → σ)) =
      Subtype.val ∘ ⇑go :=
    funext fun _ => rfl
  change rename g (rename Subtype.val (esymm _ R j)) = rename Subtype.val (esymm _ R j)
  rw [rename_rename, hcomp, ← rename_rename, esymm_isSymmetric _ _ _ go]

/-- The set of nontrivial block elementary symmetric polynomials `blockEsymm G R o j` as `o` ranges
over the `G`-orbits of `σ` and `1 ≤ j ≤ |o|`. -/
def blockEsymmSet [Finite σ] (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    Set (MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  {p | ∃ (o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) (j : ℕ),
    1 ≤ j ∧ j ≤ Nat.card {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} ∧
      p = blockEsymm G R o j}

theorem blockEsymmSet_subset_permInvariantSubalgebra [Finite σ] (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    blockEsymmSet G R ⊆ (permInvariantSubalgebra G R : Set (MvPolynomial σ R)) := by
  rintro _ ⟨o, j, -, -, rfl⟩
  exact blockEsymm_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra G o j

theorem blockEsymmSet_finite [Finite σ] (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] :
    (blockEsymmSet G R).Finite := by
  cases nonempty_fintype σ
  have : Finite (MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) := Quotient.finite _
  have hsub : blockEsymmSet G R ⊆
      (fun p : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ × Fin (Fintype.card σ + 1) =>
        blockEsymm G R p.1 p.2) '' Set.univ := by
    rintro _ ⟨o, j, -, hj, rfl⟩
    have hle : Nat.card {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} ≤ Fintype.card σ := by
      let _ : Fintype {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} := Fintype.ofFinite _
      rw [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card]
      exact Fintype.card_subtype_le _
    exact ⟨(o, ⟨j, by omega⟩), Set.mem_univ _, rfl⟩
  exact (Set.finite_univ.image _).subset hsub

end MvPolynomial

namespace MonomialOrder

open MvPolynomial

section Positive

variable {σ R : Type*}

/-- Ordering the elements of a finite subtype `S` of `σ` in strictly decreasing `m`-order of their
unit vectors `Finsupp.single i 1`. -/
private noncomputable def sortOrbitDesc (m : MonomialOrder σ) (S : Type*) [Fintype S]
    (emb : S ↪ σ) : Fin (Fintype.card S) ≃ S := by
  classical
  let f : S → m.syn := fun i => m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb i) 1)
  have hf : Function.Injective f := fun a b hab =>
    emb.injective ((Finsupp.single_left_inj (one_ne_zero : (1 : ℕ) ≠ 0)).mp (m.toSyn.injective hab))
  let img : Finset m.syn := Finset.univ.image f
  have hcard : img.card = Fintype.card S := by
    rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ hf, Finset.card_univ]
  let ord : Fin (Fintype.card S) ↪o m.syn := img.orderEmbOfFin hcard
  have hmem : ∀ k : Fin (Fintype.card S), ord k ∈ img := fun k =>
    Finset.orderEmbOfFin_mem img hcard k
  let g : Fin (Fintype.card S) → S := fun k => (Finset.mem_image.mp (hmem k.rev)).choose
  have hfg : ∀ k, f (g k) = ord k.rev := fun k => (Finset.mem_image.mp (hmem k.rev)).choose_spec.2
  have hg_inj : Function.Injective g := fun k₁ k₂ h =>
    Fin.rev_injective (ord.injective (by rw [← hfg k₁, ← hfg k₂, h]))
  exact Equiv.ofBijective g ((Fintype.bijective_iff_injective_and_card g).mpr
    ⟨hg_inj, Fintype.card_fin _⟩)

private theorem sortOrbitDesc_strictAnti (m : MonomialOrder σ) {S : Type*} [Fintype S]
    (emb : S ↪ σ) {k₁ k₂ : Fin (Fintype.card S)} (hk : k₁ < k₂) :
    Finsupp.single (emb (sortOrbitDesc m S emb k₂)) 1 ≺[m]
      Finsupp.single (emb (sortOrbitDesc m S emb k₁)) 1 := by
  classical
  let f : S → m.syn := fun i => m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb i) 1)
  have hf : Function.Injective f := fun a b hab =>
    emb.injective ((Finsupp.single_left_inj (one_ne_zero : (1 : ℕ) ≠ 0)).mp (m.toSyn.injective hab))
  let img : Finset m.syn := Finset.univ.image f
  have hcard : img.card = Fintype.card S := by
    rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ hf, Finset.card_univ]
  let ord : Fin (Fintype.card S) ↪o m.syn := img.orderEmbOfFin hcard
  have hmem : ∀ k : Fin (Fintype.card S), ord k ∈ img := fun k =>
    Finset.orderEmbOfFin_mem img hcard k
  have hfg : ∀ k, f (sortOrbitDesc m S emb k) = ord k.rev := fun k =>
    (Finset.mem_image.mp (hmem k.rev)).choose_spec.2
  change f (sortOrbitDesc m S emb k₂) < f (sortOrbitDesc m S emb k₁)
  rw [hfg k₂, hfg k₁]
  exact ord.strictMono (Fin.rev_lt_rev.mpr hk)

/-- The indicator exponent vector `∑ i ∈ T, single (emb i) 1` is injective on `Finset S`. -/
private theorem indicatorExponent_injective {S : Type*} (emb : S ↪ σ) :
    Function.Injective (fun T : Finset S => ∑ i ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb i) (1 : ℕ)) := by
  classical
  have happly : ∀ (T : Finset S) (i : S),
      (∑ j ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb j) (1 : ℕ)) (emb i) = if i ∈ T then 1 else 0 := by
    intro T i
    rw [Finsupp.finsetSum_apply]
    by_cases hi : i ∈ T
    · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single i]
      · simp [hi]
      · intro j _ hj; simp [emb.injective.ne hj]
      · intro hnot; exact absurd hi hnot
    · simp only [hi, ↓reduceIte]
      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun j hj => ?_
      have hne : j ≠ i := fun h => hi (h ▸ hj)
      simp [emb.injective.ne hne]
  intro T₁ T₂ h
  ext i
  have hi := congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) (emb i)
  rw [happly T₁ i, happly T₂ i] at hi
  by_cases h1 : i ∈ T₁ <;> by_cases h2 : i ∈ T₂ <;> simp [h1, h2] at hi ⊢

/-- Among all `j`-element subsets of a finite set `S ↪ σ`, the `j` largest elements for `m`
uniquely maximize the sum of their unit vectors. -/
private theorem sum_single_lt_topPrefix (m : MonomialOrder σ) {S : Type*} [Fintype S]
    [DecidableEq S] (emb : S ↪ σ) {j : ℕ} (hj : j ≤ Fintype.card S) {T : Finset S} (hT : T.card = j)
    (hne : T ≠ (Finset.univ.filter fun k : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (k : ℕ) < j).image
      (sortOrbitDesc m S emb)) :
    (∑ i ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) ≺[m]
      (∑ i ∈ (Finset.univ.filter fun k : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (k : ℕ) < j).image
        (sortOrbitDesc m S emb), Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) := by
  let x := sortOrbitDesc m S emb
  let K0 : Finset (Fin (Fintype.card S)) := Finset.univ.filter fun k => (k : ℕ) < j
  let T0 : Finset S := K0.image x
  have hT0_card : T0.card = j := by
    rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ x.injective]
    have hbij : K0.card = Fintype.card (Fin j) :=
      Finset.card_bij (fun k hk => ⟨(k : ℕ), (Finset.mem_filter.mp hk).2⟩)
        (fun _ _ => Finset.mem_univ _)
        (fun _ _ _ _ hab => Fin.ext (by simpa using congrArg Fin.val hab))
        (fun a _ => ⟨⟨a.1, lt_of_lt_of_le a.2 hj⟩,
          Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, a.2⟩, rfl⟩)
    rw [hbij, Fintype.card_fin]
  let A := T \ T0
  let B := T0 \ T
  have hAB_card : A.card = B.card := by
    have h1 := Finset.card_inter_add_card_sdiff T T0
    have h2 := Finset.card_inter_add_card_sdiff T0 T
    rw [Finset.inter_comm] at h2
    dsimp only [A, B]
    omega
  have hA_nonempty : A.Nonempty := by
    by_contra hemp
    rw [Finset.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty, Finset.sdiff_eq_empty_iff_subset] at hemp
    exact hne (Finset.eq_of_subset_of_card_le hemp (by change T0.card ≤ T.card; omega))
  let φ : A ≃ B := Fintype.equivOfCardEq (by simp [hAB_card])
  have hdisj1 : Disjoint (T ∩ T0) A :=
    disjoint_sdiff_self_right.mono_left Finset.inter_subset_right
  have hdisj2 : Disjoint (T0 ∩ T) B :=
    disjoint_sdiff_self_right.mono_left Finset.inter_subset_right
  have hT_eq : (T ∩ T0) ∪ A = T := by
    ext z; simp only [A, Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_inter, Finset.mem_sdiff]; tauto
  have hT0_eq : (T0 ∩ T) ∪ B = T0 := by
    ext z; simp only [B, Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_inter, Finset.mem_sdiff]; tauto
  have hdecomp1 : (∑ i ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) =
      (∑ i ∈ T ∩ T0, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) + ∑ a ∈ A, Finsupp.single (emb a) 1 := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_union hdisj1, hT_eq]
  have hdecomp2 : (∑ i ∈ T0, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) =
      (∑ i ∈ T ∩ T0, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) + ∑ b ∈ B, Finsupp.single (emb b) 1 := by
    rw [Finset.inter_comm, ← Finset.sum_union hdisj2, hT0_eq]
  have hsum_eq : ∑ b ∈ B, m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb b) 1) =
      ∑ a ∈ A.attach, m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb (φ a).1) 1) := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_attach B]
    exact (Equiv.sum_comp φ fun b : B => m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb b.1) 1)).symm
  have hpair_lt : ∀ a : A, m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb a.1) 1) <
      m.toSyn (Finsupp.single (emb (φ a).1) 1) := by
    intro a
    have ha : ¬ ((x.symm a.1 : ℕ) < j) := fun hlt =>
      (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp a.2).2 (Finset.mem_image.mpr
        ⟨x.symm a.1, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hlt⟩, x.apply_symm_apply _⟩)
    have hb : (x.symm (φ a).1 : ℕ) < j := by
      obtain ⟨k, hk, hkx⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp (φ a).2).1
      rw [← hkx, x.symm_apply_apply]
      exact (Finset.mem_filter.mp hk).2
    have hkl : x.symm (φ a).1 < x.symm a.1 := Fin.lt_def.mpr (by omega)
    have hstrict := sortOrbitDesc_strictAnti m emb hkl
    simpa only [x, Equiv.apply_symm_apply] using hstrict
  change m.toSyn (∑ i ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1) <
    m.toSyn (∑ i ∈ T0, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1)
  rw [hdecomp1, hdecomp2, map_add, map_add]
  refine add_lt_add_of_le_of_lt le_rfl ?_
  rw [map_sum, map_sum, hsum_eq, ← Finset.sum_attach A]
  exact Finset.sum_lt_sum_of_nonempty (Finset.attach_nonempty_iff.mpr hA_nonempty)
    fun a _ => hpair_lt a

/-- The leading term of `blockEsymm G R o j` (`j ≤ |o|`) is the monic product of the `j` largest
variables in the orbit `o` for `m`. -/
private theorem leadingTerm_blockEsymm [Finite σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) [CommSemiring R] [Nontrivial R]
    (o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) (j : ℕ)
    (hj : j ≤ Nat.card {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o}) :
    letI : Fintype {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} := Fintype.ofFinite _
    let x := sortOrbitDesc m {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o}
      ⟨Subtype.val, Subtype.val_injective⟩
    m.leadingTerm (blockEsymm G R o j) =
      monomial (∑ k ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin (Fintype.card _) => (k : ℕ) < j),
        Finsupp.single (x k : σ) 1) (1 : R) := by
  classical
  let _ : Fintype {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o} := Fintype.ofFinite _
  let S := {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o}
  let emb : S ↪ σ := ⟨Subtype.val, Subtype.val_injective⟩
  let x : Fin (Fintype.card S) ≃ S := sortOrbitDesc m S emb
  have hj' : j ≤ Fintype.card S := by rwa [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card] at hj
  let e : Finset S → (σ →₀ ℕ) := fun T => ∑ i ∈ T, Finsupp.single (emb i) 1
  have he_inj : Function.Injective e := indicatorExponent_injective emb
  have hsum : blockEsymm G R o j =
      ∑ T ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset S).powersetCard j, monomial (e T) (1 : R) := by
    rw [blockEsymm, esymm, map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun T _ => ?_
    rw [map_prod]
    simp only [rename_X, e, monomial_sum_one]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => rfl
  let K0 : Finset (Fin (Fintype.card S)) := Finset.univ.filter fun k => (k : ℕ) < j
  let T0 : Finset S := K0.image x
  have hT0_card : T0.card = j := by
    rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ x.injective]
    have hbij : K0.card = Fintype.card (Fin j) :=
      Finset.card_bij (fun k hk => ⟨(k : ℕ), (Finset.mem_filter.mp hk).2⟩)
        (fun _ _ => Finset.mem_univ _)
        (fun _ _ _ _ hab => Fin.ext (by simpa using congrArg Fin.val hab))
        (fun a _ => ⟨⟨a.1, lt_of_lt_of_le a.2 hj'⟩,
          Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, a.2⟩, rfl⟩)
    rw [hbij, Fintype.card_fin]
  have hT0_mem : T0 ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset S).powersetCard j :=
    Finset.mem_powersetCard.mpr ⟨Finset.subset_univ _, hT0_card⟩
  have hcoeff_T0 : (blockEsymm G R o j).coeff (e T0) = 1 := by
    rw [hsum, coeff_sum, Finset.sum_eq_single T0]
    · simp
    · intro T _ hTne
      simp [coeff_monomial, he_inj.ne hTne]
    · intro hnot
      exact absurd hT0_mem hnot
  have hdeg : m.degree (blockEsymm G R o j) = e T0 := by
    apply m.toSyn.injective
    refine le_antisymm (m.degree_le_iff.2 fun d hd => ?_) ?_
    · rw [hsum] at hd
      obtain ⟨T, hT, hdT⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp (support_sum hd)
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp (support_monomial_subset hdT)]
      rcases eq_or_ne T T0 with rfl | hne
      · exact le_rfl
      · exact (sum_single_lt_topPrefix m emb hj' (Finset.mem_powersetCard.mp hT).2 hne).le
    · apply m.le_degree
      rw [mem_support_iff, hcoeff_T0]
      exact one_ne_zero
  have heT0 : e T0 = ∑ k ∈ K0, Finsupp.single (x k : σ) 1 := by
    change (∑ i ∈ K0.image x, Finsupp.single (i : σ) 1) = _
    exact Finset.sum_image fun _ _ _ _ h => x.injective h
  rw [leadingTerm, leadingCoeff, hdeg, hcoeff_T0, heT0]

/-- If `d` is `m`-maximal in its `G`-orbit and `Equiv.swap a b ∈ G` with `X_a ≺_m X_b`, then
`d a ≤ d b`. -/
private theorem apply_le_of_swap_mem_of_mem_maxOrbitExponents [DecidableEq σ]
    (m : MonomialOrder σ) {G : Subgroup (Perm σ)} {d : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hd : d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G) {a b : σ} (hswap : swap a b ∈ G)
    (hsingle : Finsupp.single a 1 ≺[m] Finsupp.single b 1) :
    d a ≤ d b := by
  by_contra hlt
  push Not at hlt
  let k : ℕ := d a - d b
  have hk : 0 < k := Nat.sub_pos_of_lt hlt
  have hab : a ≠ b := fun h => by rw [h] at hlt; exact lt_irrefl _ hlt
  have heq : d + k • Finsupp.single b 1 =
      d.equivMapDomain (swap a b) + k • Finsupp.single a 1 := by
    ext x
    simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Finsupp.single_apply,
      Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply, Equiv.symm_swap]
    by_cases hxa : x = a
    · subst hxa
      simp only [swap_apply_left, ↓reduceIte, hab.symm, mul_zero, add_zero, mul_one, k]
      omega
    · by_cases hxb : x = b
      · subst hxb
        simp only [swap_apply_right, ↓reduceIte, hab, mul_zero, add_zero, mul_one, k]
        omega
      · simp [swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hxa hxb, Ne.symm hxa, Ne.symm hxb]
  have h1 : m.toSyn (d.equivMapDomain (swap a b)) ≤ m.toSyn d := hd (swap a b) hswap
  have h2 : k • m.toSyn (Finsupp.single a 1) < k • m.toSyn (Finsupp.single b 1) :=
    nsmul_lt_nsmul_right hk.ne' hsingle
  have hstrict : m.toSyn (d.equivMapDomain (swap a b) + k • Finsupp.single a 1) <
      m.toSyn (d + k • Finsupp.single b 1) := by
    rw [map_add, map_add, map_nsmul, map_nsmul]
    exact add_lt_add_of_le_of_lt h1 h2
  exact (ne_of_lt hstrict) (congrArg m.toSyn heq.symm)

/-- Telescoping an antitone `ℕ`-valued function on `Fin r` as a nonnegative integer combination of
prefix indicators. -/
private theorem antitone_fin_eq_sum_prefix {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → ℕ) (hc : Antitone c) :
    ∃ w : Fin r → ℕ, ∀ i : Fin r,
      c i = ∑ k ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i ≤ k), w k := by
  refine ⟨fun k => if h : (k : ℕ) + 1 < r then c k - c ⟨k + 1, h⟩ else c k, fun i => ?_⟩
  suffices ∀ n (i : Fin r), r - 1 - (i : ℕ) = n →
      c i = ∑ k ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i ≤ k),
        if h : (k : ℕ) + 1 < r then c k - c ⟨k + 1, h⟩ else c k from
    this (r - 1 - (i : ℕ)) i rfl
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro i hi
    have hlast : ¬ (i : ℕ) + 1 < r := by omega
    have hfilt : Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i ≤ k) = {i} := by
      ext k
      simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and, Finset.mem_singleton, Fin.le_def,
        Fin.ext_iff]
      omega
    rw [hfilt, Finset.sum_singleton]
    simp [hlast]
  | succ m ih =>
    intro i hi
    have hlt : (i : ℕ) + 1 < r := by omega
    let i' : Fin r := ⟨i + 1, hlt⟩
    have hi' : r - 1 - (i' : ℕ) = m := by simp only [i']; omega
    have hfilt : Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i ≤ k) =
        insert i (Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i' ≤ k)) := by
      ext k
      simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and, Finset.mem_insert, Fin.le_def,
        Fin.ext_iff, i']
      omega
    have hnot : i ∉ Finset.univ.filter (fun k : Fin r => i' ≤ k) := by
      simp [Fin.le_def, i']
    rw [hfilt, Finset.sum_insert hnot]
    simp only [hlt, ↓reduceDIte]
    rw [← ih i' hi']
    exact (Nat.sub_add_cancel (hc (Fin.le_def.mpr (by simp)))).symm

/-- On a single `G`-orbit `o`, any `m`-maximal exponent for a transposition-generated subgroup `G`
telescopes as a nonnegative integer combination of prefix sums of the sorted orbit variables. -/
private theorem orbit_part_monomial_mem_adjoin [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [Nontrivial R]
    (hG : Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} = G)
    {d : σ →₀ ℕ} (hd : d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G) (o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ)
    (orb : Finset σ) (horb_mem : ∀ i : σ, i ∈ orb ↔ Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o) :
    monomial (∑ i ∈ orb, Finsupp.single i (d i)) (1 : R) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin R (m.leadingTerm '' blockEsymmSet G R) := by
  let S := {i : σ // Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o}
  let _ : Fintype S := Fintype.ofFinite _
  let emb : S ↪ σ := ⟨Subtype.val, Subtype.val_injective⟩
  let x : Fin (Fintype.card S) ≃ S := sortOrbitDesc m S emb
  have hanti : Antitone (fun k : Fin (Fintype.card S) => d (x k : σ)) := fun k₁ k₂ hk => by
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le hk with rfl | hlt
    · exact le_rfl
    · have horb : MulAction.orbitRel G σ (x k₂ : σ) (x k₁ : σ) :=
        Quotient.exact ((x k₂).2.trans (x k₁).2.symm)
      exact apply_le_of_swap_mem_of_mem_maxOrbitExponents m hd
        (G.swap_mem_of_orbitRel_of_closure_isSwap_eq hG horb)
        (sortOrbitDesc_strictAnti m emb hlt)
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := antitone_fin_eq_sum_prefix (fun k => d (x k : σ)) hanti
  have hsum_eq :
      (∑ i ∈ orb, Finsupp.single i (d i)) =
      ∑ k : Fin (Fintype.card S),
        w k • ∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
          Finsupp.single (x t : σ) 1 := by
    ext a
    rw [Finsupp.finsetSum_apply, Finsupp.finsetSum_apply]
    simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Finsupp.finsetSum_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    by_cases ha : Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) a = o
    · let t₀ : Fin (Fintype.card S) := x.symm ⟨a, ha⟩
      have hlhs : (∑ i ∈ orb, if i = a then d i else 0) = d a := by
        rw [Finset.sum_eq_single a]
        · simp
        · intro i _ hia; simp [hia]
        · intro hnot; exact absurd ((horb_mem a).mpr ha) hnot
      rw [hlhs, show d a = d (x t₀ : σ) by simp [t₀], hw t₀]
      have hcond : ∀ t : Fin (Fintype.card S), ((x t : σ) = a) ↔ t = t₀ := fun t =>
        ⟨fun h => x.injective (Subtype.ext (h.trans (by simp [t₀]))),
         fun h => by subst h; simp [t₀]⟩
      have hinner : ∀ k : Fin (Fintype.card S),
          w k * (∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
            if (x t : σ) = a then 1 else 0) = if t₀ ≤ k then w k else 0 := fun k => by
        by_cases hk : t₀ ≤ k
        · simp only [hk, ↓reduceIte]
          rw [Finset.sum_eq_single t₀]
          · simp [hcond]
          · intro t _ htt; simp [(hcond t).not.mpr htt]
          · intro hnot
            exact absurd (Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ t₀,
              Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Fin.le_def.mp hk)⟩) hnot
        · simp only [hk, ↓reduceIte]
          have hzero : (∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter
              (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
              if (x t : σ) = a then 1 else 0) = 0 :=
            Finset.sum_eq_zero fun t ht => by
              have hne : t ≠ t₀ := fun h => hk (by
                subst h; exact Fin.le_def.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_filter.mp ht).2))
              simp [(hcond t).not.mpr hne]
          rw [hzero, mul_zero]
      simp_rw [hinner]
      rw [← Finset.sum_filter]
    · rw [Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi => by
        have hne : i ≠ a := fun h => ha (h ▸ (horb_mem i).mp hi); simp [hne]]
      symm
      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ => ?_
      have hzero : (∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter
          (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
          if (x t : σ) = a then 1 else 0) = 0 :=
        Finset.sum_eq_zero fun t _ => by
          have hne : (x t : σ) ≠ a := fun h => ha (h ▸ (x t).2); simp [hne]
      rw [hzero, mul_zero]
  rw [hsum_eq, monomial_sum_one]
  refine Subalgebra.prod_mem _ fun k _ => ?_
  have hpow : monomial (w k • ∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter
        (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
        Finsupp.single (x t : σ) 1) (1 : R) =
      (monomial (∑ t ∈ Finset.univ.filter
        (fun t : Fin (Fintype.card S) => (t : ℕ) < (k : ℕ) + 1),
        Finsupp.single (x t : σ) 1) (1 : R)) ^ w k := by
    rw [monomial_pow, one_pow]
  rw [hpow]
  refine Subalgebra.pow_mem _ ?_ _
  have hcard_le : (k : ℕ) + 1 ≤ Nat.card S := by
    rw [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card]; exact Nat.succ_le_of_lt k.isLt
  rw [← m.leadingTerm_blockEsymm (R := R) G o ((k : ℕ) + 1) hcard_le]
  exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨blockEsymm G R o ((k : ℕ) + 1),
    ⟨o, (k : ℕ) + 1, Nat.succ_pos _, hcard_le, rfl⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **Positive direction of the permutation SAGBI criterion.** If `G ≤ Equiv.Perm σ` is generated by
transpositions on a finite type `σ`, then for every monomial order `m` and every commutative
semiring `R`, the finite set `MvPolynomial.blockEsymmSet G R` of block elementary symmetric
polynomials is an `m`-SAGBI basis of `MvPolynomial.permInvariantSubalgebra G R`. -/
theorem isSAGBIBasis_blockEsymmSet [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*) [CommSemiring R]
    (hG : Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} = G) :
    m.IsSAGBIBasis (blockEsymmSet G R) (permInvariantSubalgebra G R) := by
  classical
  cases nonempty_fintype σ
  rw [isSAGBIBasis_iff_initialAlgebra_le]
  refine ⟨blockEsymmSet_subset_permInvariantSubalgebra G R, ?_⟩
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with hsub | _
  · intro p _
    rw [Subsingleton.elim p 0]
    exact zero_mem _
  rw [initialAlgebra_def, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
  rcases eq_or_ne p 0 with rfl | hp0
  · simp
  let d : σ →₀ ℕ := m.degree p
  have hd : d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G := fun g hg =>
    m.equivMapDomain_degree_le_of_mem_permInvariantSubalgebra hp hp0 hg
  let _ : Fintype (MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  let orb : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ → Finset σ :=
    fun o => Finset.univ.filter fun i : σ => Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o
  have horb_mem : ∀ o i, i ∈ orb o ↔ Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) i = o := fun o i => by
    simp [orb]
  have hd_eq : d = ∑ o : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G σ,
      ∑ i ∈ orb o, Finsupp.single i (d i) := by
    ext a
    rw [Finsupp.finsetSum_apply]
    simp_rw [Finsupp.finsetSum_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single (Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ) a)]
    · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single a]
      · simp
      · intro i _ hia; simp [hia]
      · intro hnot; exact absurd ((horb_mem _ a).mpr rfl) hnot
    · intro o _ ho
      exact Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi => by
        have hia : i ≠ a := fun h => ho (h ▸ (horb_mem o i).mp hi).symm
        simp [hia]
    · intro hnot; exact absurd (Finset.mem_univ _) hnot
  have hmon : monomial d (1 : R) ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (m.leadingTerm '' blockEsymmSet G R) := by
    rw [hd_eq, monomial_sum_one]
    exact Subalgebra.prod_mem _ fun o _ =>
      orbit_part_monomial_mem_adjoin m G R hG hd o (orb o) (horb_mem o)
  have hlt_eq : m.leadingTerm p = m.leadingCoeff p • monomial d (1 : R) := by
    rw [leadingTerm, smul_monomial, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  rw [hlt_eq]
  exact Subalgebra.smul_mem _ hmon _

end Positive

/-! ### Negative direction: rational polyhedral cone and hyperplane crossing -/

section Negative

variable {σ : Type*}

/-- Embed an exponent vector `σ →₀ ℕ` into the rational vector space `σ → ℚ`. -/
private def ratEmbed : (σ →₀ ℕ) →+ (σ → ℚ) where
  toFun d i := (d i : ℚ)
  map_zero' := funext fun _ => by simp
  map_add' a b := funext fun _ => by simp

private theorem ratEmbed_injective : Function.Injective (ratEmbed (σ := σ)) := by
  intro a b h
  ext i
  exact Nat.cast_injective (congrFun h i)

/-- The left permutation action on `σ → ℚ` given by `(permAct g v) i = v (g⁻¹ i)`. -/
private def permAct (g : Perm σ) (v : σ → ℚ) : σ → ℚ :=
  fun i => v (g.symm i)

private theorem permAct_one (v : σ → ℚ) : permAct 1 v = v :=
  funext fun _ => rfl

private theorem permAct_mul (g₁ g₂ : Perm σ) (v : σ → ℚ) :
    permAct (g₁ * g₂) v = permAct g₁ (permAct g₂ v) :=
  funext fun _ => rfl

private theorem permAct_add (g : Perm σ) (u v : σ → ℚ) :
    permAct g (u + v) = permAct g u + permAct g v :=
  funext fun _ => rfl

private theorem permAct_smul (g : Perm σ) (c : ℚ) (v : σ → ℚ) :
    permAct g (c • v) = c • permAct g v :=
  funext fun _ => rfl

private theorem permAct_ratEmbed (g : Perm σ) (d : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    permAct g (ratEmbed d) = ratEmbed (d.equivMapDomain g) :=
  funext fun i => by simp [permAct, ratEmbed, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply]

private def permActLinearEquiv (g : Perm σ) : (σ → ℚ) ≃ₗ[ℚ] (σ → ℚ) where
  toFun := permAct g
  invFun := permAct g⁻¹
  left_inv v := funext fun i => by simp [permAct, Equiv.Perm.inv_def]
  right_inv v := funext fun i => by simp [permAct, Equiv.Perm.inv_def]
  map_add' := permAct_add g
  map_smul' := permAct_smul g

/-- The rational pointed cone generated by the image of `m.maxOrbitExponents G`. -/
private noncomputable def maxOrbitCone (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) :
    PointedCone ℚ (σ → ℚ) :=
  PointedCone.hull ℚ (ratEmbed '' (m.maxOrbitExponents G : Set (σ →₀ ℕ)))

private theorem fg_maxOrbitCone (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    (hfg : (m.maxOrbitExponents G).FG) : (maxOrbitCone m G).FG := by
  classical
  rw [AddSubmonoid.fg_iff] at hfg
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hSfin⟩ := hfg
  have heq : maxOrbitCone m G = PointedCone.hull ℚ (ratEmbed '' S) := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rw [maxOrbitCone, PointedCone.hull, Submodule.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
      have hd' : d ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure S := hS.symm ▸ hd
      clear hd
      induction hd' using AddSubmonoid.closure_induction with
      | mem a ha => exact PointedCone.subset_hull ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
      | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
      | add a b _ _ iha ihb => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem iha ihb
    · refine Submodule.span_mono ?_
      rintro _ ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨a, hS ▸ AddSubmonoid.subset_closure ha, rfl⟩
  rw [heq]
  exact Submodule.fg_span (hSfin.image ratEmbed)

/-- A nonnegative rational scaled by a multiple of its denominator is a natural number. -/
private theorem rat_nonneg_mul_nat_eq_nat {q : ℚ} (hq : 0 ≤ q) {N : ℕ} (hdvd : q.den ∣ N) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, (N : ℚ) * q = (k : ℚ) := by
  obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hdvd
  have hnum : 0 ≤ q.num := Rat.num_nonneg.mpr hq
  refine ⟨r * q.num.toNat, ?_⟩
  have hden0 : (q.den : ℚ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr q.den_nz
  have hnum_eq : ((q.num.toNat : ℕ) : ℚ) = (q.num : ℚ) := by
    exact_mod_cast Int.toNat_of_nonneg hnum
  calc ((q.den * r : ℕ) : ℚ) * q
      = (q.den : ℚ) * (r : ℚ) * ((q.num : ℚ) / (q.den : ℚ)) := by
          rw [Nat.cast_mul, Rat.num_div_den]
    _ = (r : ℚ) * (q.num : ℚ) := by field_simp [hden0]
    _ = ((r * q.num.toNat : ℕ) : ℚ) := by rw [Nat.cast_mul, hnum_eq]

/-- `m.maxOrbitExponents G` is saturated under positive scalar multiplication, so integer points in
`maxOrbitCone m G` lie in `m.maxOrbitExponents G`. -/
private theorem ratEmbed_mem_maxOrbitCone_iff (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    (d : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    ratEmbed d ∈ maxOrbitCone m G ↔ d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G := by
  constructor
  · intro hd
    rw [maxOrbitCone, PointedCone.mem_hull_set] at hd
    obtain ⟨c, hc_supp, hc_nonneg, hc_sum⟩ := hd
    let N : ℕ := ∏ y ∈ c.support, (c y).den
    have hNpos : 0 < N := Finset.prod_pos fun y _ => (c y).pos
    have hscaled : ∀ y ∈ c.support, ∃ k : ℕ, (N : ℚ) * c y = (k : ℚ) := fun y hy =>
      rat_nonneg_mul_nat_eq_nat (hc_nonneg y) (Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem _ hy)
    have hpre : ∀ y ∈ c.support, ∃ a ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G, ratEmbed a = y := fun y hy =>
      hc_supp (Finset.mem_coe.mpr hy)
    choose k hk using hscaled
    choose a ha haeq using hpre
    let d' : σ →₀ ℕ := ∑ y ∈ c.support.attach, k y.1 y.2 • a y.1 y.2
    have hd'_mem : d' ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G :=
      sum_mem fun y _ => nsmul_mem (ha y.1 y.2) _
    have hNd : N • d = d' := by
      apply ratEmbed_injective
      have hcast : ∀ (n : ℕ) (v : σ → ℚ), n • v = (n : ℚ) • v := fun n v =>
        funext fun i => by simp
      rw [map_nsmul, hcast, ← hc_sum, Finsupp.sum, Finset.smul_sum, map_sum,
        ← Finset.sum_attach c.support]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => ?_
      rw [smul_smul, hk y.1 y.2, map_nsmul, hcast, haeq y.1 y.2]
    intro g hg
    have h1 := hd'_mem g hg
    rw [← hNd] at h1
    have hmap : (N • d).equivMapDomain g = N • d.equivMapDomain g := by
      ext i; simp [Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply]
    rw [hmap, map_nsmul, map_nsmul] at h1
    by_contra hnot
    push Not at hnot
    exact not_lt_of_ge h1 (nsmul_lt_nsmul_right hNpos.ne' hnot)
  · intro hd
    exact PointedCone.subset_hull ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩

/-- Any nonnegative rational vector `x : σ → ℚ` scales to `ratEmbed d` for some `d : σ →₀ ℕ`. -/
private theorem exists_nat_smul_eq_ratEmbed [Finite σ] {x : σ → ℚ} (hx : ∀ i, 0 ≤ x i) :
    ∃ (D : ℕ) (d : σ →₀ ℕ), 0 < D ∧ (D : ℚ) • x = ratEmbed d := by
  cases nonempty_fintype σ
  let D : ℕ := ∏ i : σ, (x i).den
  have hDpos : 0 < D := Finset.prod_pos fun i _ => (x i).pos
  have hscaled : ∀ i : σ, ∃ k : ℕ, (D : ℚ) * x i = (k : ℚ) := fun i =>
    rat_nonneg_mul_nat_eq_nat (hx i) (Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ i))
  choose k hk using hscaled
  refine ⟨D, Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm k, hDpos, funext fun i => ?_⟩
  simpa [ratEmbed, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] using hk i

/-- **Covering:** every nonnegative rational vector can be moved into `maxOrbitCone m G` by some
element of `G`. -/
private theorem exists_permAct_mem_maxOrbitCone [Finite σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) {x : σ → ℚ} (hx : ∀ i, 0 ≤ x i) :
    ∃ g ∈ G, permAct g x ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := by
  classical
  let _ : Fintype G := Fintype.ofFinite G
  obtain ⟨D, d, hDpos, hDd⟩ := exists_nat_smul_eq_ratEmbed hx
  obtain ⟨g₀, -, hg₀max⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image Finset.univ
    (fun g : G => m.toSyn (d.equivMapDomain (g : Perm σ)))
    (Finset.univ_nonempty_iff.mpr ⟨⟨1, G.one_mem⟩⟩)
  have hd'_mem : d.equivMapDomain (g₀ : Perm σ) ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G := by
    intro h hh
    rw [← Finsupp.equivMapDomain_trans]
    exact hg₀max ⟨h * g₀, G.mul_mem hh g₀.2⟩ (Finset.mem_univ _)
  refine ⟨(g₀ : Perm σ), g₀.2, ?_⟩
  have hinv_pos : (0 : ℚ) ≤ (D : ℚ)⁻¹ := inv_nonneg.mpr (Nat.cast_nonneg D)
  have heq : permAct (g₀ : Perm σ) x =
      (D : ℚ)⁻¹ • ratEmbed (d.equivMapDomain (g₀ : Perm σ)) := by
    rw [← permAct_ratEmbed, ← hDd, permAct_smul]
    ext i
    have hD0 : (D : ℚ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr hDpos.ne'
    simp [permAct, hD0]
  rw [heq]
  exact PointedCone.smul_mem _ hinv_pos ((ratEmbed_mem_maxOrbitCone_iff m G _).mpr hd'_mem)

/-- **Disjointness on non-fixed points:** if a nonnegative rational vector `x` and its `g`-translate
both lie in `maxOrbitCone m G` (`g ∈ G`), then `g` fixes `x`. -/
private theorem permAct_eq_self_of_mem_maxOrbitCone [Finite σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ)
    (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) {x : σ → ℚ} (hx : ∀ i, 0 ≤ x i) {g : Perm σ} (hg : g ∈ G)
    (hxC : x ∈ maxOrbitCone m G) (hgxC : permAct g x ∈ maxOrbitCone m G) :
    permAct g x = x := by
  obtain ⟨D, d, hDpos, hDd⟩ := exists_nat_smul_eq_ratEmbed hx
  have hDnonneg : (0 : ℚ) ≤ (D : ℚ) := Nat.cast_nonneg D
  have hd_mem : d ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G := by
    rw [← ratEmbed_mem_maxOrbitCone_iff, ← hDd]
    exact PointedCone.smul_mem _ hDnonneg hxC
  have hgd_mem : d.equivMapDomain g ∈ m.maxOrbitExponents G := by
    rw [← ratEmbed_mem_maxOrbitCone_iff, ← permAct_ratEmbed, ← hDd, permAct_smul]
    exact PointedCone.smul_mem _ hDnonneg hgxC
  have hle1 : d.equivMapDomain g ≼[m] d := hd_mem g hg
  have hle2 : d ≼[m] d.equivMapDomain g := by
    have h := hgd_mem g⁻¹ (G.inv_mem hg)
    rw [← Finsupp.equivMapDomain_trans] at h
    have hid : g.trans g⁻¹ = Equiv.refl σ := Equiv.self_trans_symm g
    rwa [hid, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_refl] at h
  have hdeq : d.equivMapDomain g = d := m.toSyn.injective (le_antisymm hle1 hle2)
  have hscale : (D : ℚ) • permAct g x = (D : ℚ) • x := by
    rw [← permAct_smul, hDd, permAct_ratEmbed, hdeq]
  exact smul_right_injective (σ → ℚ) (Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr hDpos.ne') hscale

/-- The coordinate-equality hyperplane `{v : σ → ℚ | v a = v b}`. -/
private def coordEqHyperplane (a b : σ) : Submodule ℚ (σ → ℚ) :=
  LinearMap.ker ((LinearMap.proj a : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj b)

private theorem mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff (a b : σ) (v : σ → ℚ) :
    v ∈ coordEqHyperplane a b ↔ v a = v b := by
  simp [coordEqHyperplane, sub_eq_zero]

/-- Distinct pairs of indices define distinct coordinate-equality hyperplanes (up to swapping the
pair). -/
private theorem eq_or_eq_of_coordEqHyperplane_eq {a b c d : σ}
    (hcd : c ≠ d) (heq : coordEqHyperplane a b = coordEqHyperplane c d) :
    c = a ∨ c = b := by
  classical
  by_contra hneither
  push Not at hneither
  have hmem : Pi.single c (1 : ℚ) ∈ coordEqHyperplane a b := by
    rw [mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hneither.1.symm,
      Pi.single_eq_of_ne hneither.2.symm]
  rw [heq, mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff, Pi.single_eq_same, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hcd.symm] at hmem
  exact one_ne_zero hmem

/-- If two hyperplanes `ker φ₁ ≠ ker φ₂` both avoid `p`, then `span {p} ⊔ (ker φ₁ ⊓ ker φ₂) ≠ ⊤`. -/
private theorem span_sup_inf_ker_ne_top {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V]
    {φ₁ φ₂ : Module.Dual ℚ V} {p : V}
    (hne : LinearMap.ker φ₁ ≠ LinearMap.ker φ₂)
    (hp₁ : p ∉ LinearMap.ker φ₁) (hp₂ : p ∉ LinearMap.ker φ₂) :
    Submodule.span ℚ {p} ⊔ (LinearMap.ker φ₁ ⊓ LinearMap.ker φ₂) ≠ ⊤ := by
  let ψ : Module.Dual ℚ V := (φ₂ p) • φ₁ - (φ₁ p) • φ₂
  have hle : Submodule.span ℚ {p} ⊔ (LinearMap.ker φ₁ ⊓ LinearMap.ker φ₂) ≤ LinearMap.ker ψ := by
    refine sup_le ?_ ?_
    · rw [Submodule.span_singleton_le_iff_mem, LinearMap.mem_ker]
      simp [ψ, mul_comm]
    · rintro v ⟨hv₁, hv₂⟩
      rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]
      simp [ψ, LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hv₁, LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hv₂]
  have hψ0 : ψ ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    apply hne
    ext v
    have hv := LinearMap.congr_fun h0 v
    simp only [ψ, LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, LinearMap.zero_apply,
      sub_eq_zero] at hv
    have h1 : φ₁ p ≠ 0 := by simpa [LinearMap.mem_ker] using hp₁
    have h2 : φ₂ p ≠ 0 := by simpa [LinearMap.mem_ker] using hp₂
    simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker]
    constructor
    · intro hφ1
      have hmul : φ₁ p * φ₂ v = 0 := by rw [← hv, hφ1, mul_zero]
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hmul).resolve_left h1
    · intro hφ2
      have hmul : φ₂ p * φ₁ v = 0 := by rw [hv, hφ2, mul_zero]
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hmul).resolve_left h2
  intro htop
  rw [htop, top_le_iff] at hle
  exact hψ0 (LinearMap.ker_eq_top.mp hle)

/-- Perturb a point `q` along a direction avoiding a finite family of submodules so that finitely
many strictly positive linear conditions are preserved while avoiding every submodule in the
family. -/
private theorem exists_perturb_pos_and_notMem {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V]
    (q : V) (L : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ V)) (hL : ∀ φ ∈ L, 0 < φ q)
    (ℬ : Finset (Submodule ℚ V)) (hℬ : ∀ K ∈ ℬ, K ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ q' : V, (∀ φ ∈ L, 0 < φ q') ∧ (∀ K ∈ ℬ, q' ∉ K) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := Submodule.exists_forall_notMem_of_forall_ne_top
    (fun K : ℬ => (K : Submodule ℚ V)) (fun K => hℬ K.1 K.2)
  let bounds : Finset ℚ := insert 1 (L.image fun φ => φ q / (|φ v| + 1))
  let ε : ℚ := bounds.min' (Finset.insert_nonempty _ _)
  have hε : 0 < ε := by
    have hmem : ε ∈ bounds := Finset.min'_mem bounds (Finset.insert_nonempty _ _)
    rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hmem with h1 | h2
    · rw [h1]; exact zero_lt_one
    · obtain ⟨φ, hφ, hφeq⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp h2
      rw [← hφeq]
      exact div_pos (hL φ hφ) (by positivity)
  have hbad_fin : (⋃ K ∈ ℬ, {s : ℚ | q + s • v ∈ K}).Finite := by
    refine ℬ.finite_toSet.biUnion fun K hK => Set.Subsingleton.finite fun s₁ hs₁ s₂ hs₂ => ?_
    by_contra hne
    have hdiff : (s₁ - s₂) • v ∈ K := by
      have hsub := K.sub_mem hs₁ hs₂
      have heq : (q + s₁ • v) - (q + s₂ • v) = (s₁ - s₂) • v := by module
      rwa [heq] at hsub
    have hvK : v ∈ K := by
      have hsmul := K.smul_mem (s₁ - s₂)⁻¹ hdiff
      rwa [smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ (sub_ne_zero.mpr hne), one_smul] at hsmul
    exact hv ⟨K, hK⟩ hvK
  obtain ⟨s, hsIoo, hsnot⟩ := (Set.Ioo_infinite hε).exists_notMem_finite hbad_fin
  refine ⟨q + s • v, fun φ hφ => ?_, fun K hK hmem => hsnot (Set.mem_biUnion hK hmem)⟩
  have hs_lt : s < φ q / (|φ v| + 1) := lt_of_lt_of_le hsIoo.2
    (Finset.min'_le bounds _ (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hφ)))
  have hdenom : 0 < |φ v| + 1 := by positivity
  have hmul : s * (|φ v| + 1) < φ q := (lt_div_iff₀ hdenom).mp hs_lt
  have hle : s * (-(φ v)) ≤ s * |φ v| :=
    mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (neg_le_abs (φ v)) hsIoo.1.le
  have hlt2 : s * |φ v| < s * (|φ v| + 1) := by linarith [hsIoo.1]
  rw [map_add, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
  linarith

/-- Rational affine sign preservation: if `f(t) = (1 - t) * u + t * v` is strictly positive at an
interior point `m ∈ (a, b)` and never vanishes on `(a, b)`, then `0 ≤ f a` and `0 ≤ f b`. -/
private theorem rational_affine_nonneg_of_no_zero {a m b u v : ℚ}
    (ham : a < m) (hmb : m < b)
    (hm : 0 < (1 - m) * u + m * v)
    (hno : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo a b, (1 - t) * u + t * v ≠ 0) :
    0 ≤ (1 - a) * u + a * v ∧ 0 ≤ (1 - b) * u + b * v := by
  constructor
  · by_contra hlt
    push Not at hlt
    set fa := (1 - a) * u + a * v
    set fm := (1 - m) * u + m * v
    have hden : 0 < fm - fa := by linarith
    let t : ℚ := (a * fm + m * (-fa)) / (fm - fa)
    have hat : a < t := (lt_div_iff₀ hden).mpr (by nlinarith)
    have htm : t < m := (div_lt_iff₀ hden).mpr (by nlinarith)
    have hzero : (1 - t) * u + t * v = 0 := by
      have hden0 : fm - fa ≠ 0 := hden.ne'
      have ht : (fm - fa) * t = a * fm + m * (-fa) := mul_div_cancel₀ _ hden0
      have hmul : (fm - fa) * ((1 - t) * u + t * v) = 0 := by
        calc (fm - fa) * ((1 - t) * u + t * v)
            = (fm - fa) * u + ((fm - fa) * t) * (v - u) := by ring
          _ = (fm - fa) * u + (a * fm + m * (-fa)) * (v - u) := by rw [ht]
          _ = 0 := by simp only [fa, fm]; ring
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hmul).resolve_left hden0
    exact hno t ⟨hat, lt_trans htm hmb⟩ hzero
  · by_contra hlt
    push Not at hlt
    set fb := (1 - b) * u + b * v
    set fm := (1 - m) * u + m * v
    have hden : 0 < fm - fb := by linarith
    let t : ℚ := (m * (-fb) + b * fm) / (fm - fb)
    have hmt : m < t := (lt_div_iff₀ hden).mpr (by nlinarith)
    have htb : t < b := (div_lt_iff₀ hden).mpr (by nlinarith)
    have hzero : (1 - t) * u + t * v = 0 := by
      have hden0 : fm - fb ≠ 0 := hden.ne'
      have ht : (fm - fb) * t = m * (-fb) + b * fm := mul_div_cancel₀ _ hden0
      have hmul : (fm - fb) * ((1 - t) * u + t * v) = 0 := by
        calc (fm - fb) * ((1 - t) * u + t * v)
            = (fm - fb) * u + ((fm - fb) * t) * (v - u) := by ring
          _ = (fm - fb) * u + (m * (-fb) + b * fm) * (v - u) := by rw [ht]
          _ = 0 := by simp only [fb, fm]; ring
      exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hmul).resolve_left hden0
    exact hno t ⟨lt_trans ham hmt, htb⟩ hzero

/-- If a permutation `τ` fixes a point `x : σ → ℚ` that lies on at most one coordinate-equality
hyperplane, then `τ = 1` or `τ` is a transposition. -/
private theorem eq_one_or_isSwap_of_permAct_eq [DecidableEq σ] {τ : Perm σ} {x : σ → ℚ}
    (hfix : permAct τ x = x)
    (huniq : ∀ a b c d : σ, a ≠ b → c ≠ d →
      x ∈ coordEqHyperplane a b → x ∈ coordEqHyperplane c d →
      coordEqHyperplane a b = coordEqHyperplane c d) :
    τ = 1 ∨ τ.IsSwap := by
  rcases eq_or_ne τ 1 with rfl | hne
  · exact Or.inl rfl
  · right
    have hne_inv : τ⁻¹ ≠ 1 := fun h => hne (inv_eq_one.mp h)
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : ∃ a : σ, τ⁻¹ a ≠ a := by
      by_contra hall
      push Not at hall
      exact hne_inv (Equiv.ext hall)
    let b : σ := τ⁻¹ a
    have hab : a ≠ b := ha.symm
    have hxab : x ∈ coordEqHyperplane a b := by
      rw [mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff]; exact (congrFun hfix a).symm
    have hmoved : ∀ z : σ, τ⁻¹ z ≠ z → z = a ∨ z = b := fun z hz => by
      have hxzz : x ∈ coordEqHyperplane z (τ⁻¹ z) := by
        rw [mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff]; exact (congrFun hfix z).symm
      exact eq_or_eq_of_coordEqHyperplane_eq hz.symm (huniq a b z (τ⁻¹ z) hab hz.symm hxab hxzz)
    have hinv_b : τ⁻¹ b = a := by
      have hnb : τ⁻¹ b ≠ b := fun h => hab (τ⁻¹.injective h).symm
      exact (hmoved (τ⁻¹ b) (fun h => hnb (τ⁻¹.injective h))).resolve_right hnb
    have hinv_eq : τ⁻¹ = swap a b := by
      ext z
      rcases eq_or_ne z a with rfl | hza
      · simp [b]
      · rcases eq_or_ne z b with rfl | hzb
        · simp [hinv_b]
        · rw [swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hza hzb]
          by_contra hz
          exact (hmoved z hz).elim hza hzb
    have hτ_eq : τ = swap a b := by
      calc τ = (τ⁻¹)⁻¹ := (inv_inv τ).symm
        _ = (swap a b)⁻¹ := congrArg Inv.inv hinv_eq
        _ = swap a b := Equiv.symm_swap a b
    exact ⟨a, b, hab, hτ_eq⟩

/-- A permutation fixing a point outside all coordinate-equality hyperplanes is the identity. -/
private theorem eq_one_of_permAct_eq_of_notMem_coordEq {τ : Perm σ} {x : σ → ℚ}
    (hfix : permAct τ x = x)
    (hout : ∀ a b : σ, a ≠ b → x ∉ coordEqHyperplane a b) :
    τ = 1 := by
  ext i
  by_contra hne
  have hne' : i ≠ τ.symm i := fun heq => by
    have := congrArg τ heq
    rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at this
    exact hne (by simpa using this)
  exact hout i (τ.symm i) hne' ((mem_coordEqHyperplane_iff i (τ.symm i) x).mpr
    (congrFun hfix i).symm)

/-- Walking along a generic rational segment `γ t = (1 - t) • p₁ + t • q₁` between `p₁ ∈ C` and
`q₁ ∈ g • C` factors `g` as a product of transpositions in `G`. -/
private theorem mem_closure_isSwap_of_generic_segment [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ]
    (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    (F : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)))
    (hC_iff : ∀ x : σ → ℚ, x ∈ maxOrbitCone m G ↔ ∀ ℓ ∈ F, 0 ≤ ℓ x)
    (Φ : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)))
    (hwall : ∀ h ∈ G, ∀ ℓ ∈ F, ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv h⁻¹).toLinearMap ∈ Φ)
    (heq_mem : ∀ a b : σ, a ≠ b →
      ((LinearMap.proj a : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj b) ∈ Φ)
    {g : Perm σ} (hg : g ∈ G) {p₁ q₁ : σ → ℚ}
    (hp₁_pos : ∀ i, 0 < p₁ i) (hq₁_pos : ∀ i, 0 < q₁ i)
    (hp₁C : p₁ ∈ maxOrbitCone m G) (hq₁_gC : permAct g⁻¹ q₁ ∈ maxOrbitCone m G)
    (hp₁_out : ∀ φ ∈ Φ, φ p₁ ≠ 0) (hq₁_out : ∀ φ ∈ Φ, φ q₁ ≠ 0)
    (hγ_uniq : ∀ (t : ℚ) {φ₁ φ₂ : Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)}, φ₁ ∈ Φ → φ₂ ∈ Φ →
      φ₁ ((1 - t) • p₁ + t • q₁) = 0 → φ₂ ((1 - t) • p₁ + t • q₁) = 0 →
      LinearMap.ker φ₁ = LinearMap.ker φ₂) :
    g ∈ Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} := by
  classical
  let γ : ℚ → (σ → ℚ) := fun t => (1 - t) • p₁ + t • q₁
  have hγ_pos : ∀ t : ℚ, 0 ≤ t → t ≤ 1 → ∀ i, 0 < γ t i := fun t ht0 ht1 i => by
    simp only [γ, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le ht0 with rfl | ht0'
    · simpa using hp₁_pos i
    · have : 0 ≤ 1 - t := sub_nonneg.mpr ht1
      nlinarith [hp₁_pos i, hq₁_pos i]
  let crossTimes : Finset ℚ :=
    ((Φ.filter fun φ => φ p₁ ≠ φ q₁).image fun φ => φ p₁ / (φ p₁ - φ q₁)).filter
      fun t => 0 < t ∧ t < 1
  let nodes : Finset ℚ := insert 0 (insert 1 crossTimes)
  have h0_mem : (0 : ℚ) ∈ nodes := Finset.mem_insert_self _ _
  have h1_mem : (1 : ℚ) ∈ nodes := Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_insert_self _ _)
  have hnodes_card : 2 ≤ nodes.card := by
    refine le_trans (by decide : 2 ≤ ({0, 1} : Finset ℚ).card) (Finset.card_le_card fun x hx => ?_)
    rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hx with rfl | hx'
    · exact h0_mem
    · rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp hx']; exact h1_mem
  let k : ℕ := nodes.card - 2
  have hk_eq : nodes.card = k + 2 := by omega
  let c : Fin (k + 2) ↪o ℚ := nodes.orderEmbOfFin hk_eq
  have hrange : (nodes : Set ℚ) = Set.range c := (Finset.range_orderEmbOfFin nodes hk_eq).symm
  have hc_mem : ∀ j, c j ∈ nodes := fun j => Finset.orderEmbOfFin_mem nodes hk_eq j
  have hc_bounds : ∀ t ∈ nodes, 0 ≤ t ∧ t ≤ 1 := fun t ht => by
    rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp ht with rfl | ht'
    · exact ⟨le_rfl, zero_le_one⟩
    · rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp ht' with rfl | ht''
      · exact ⟨zero_le_one, le_rfl⟩
      · have := (Finset.mem_filter.mp ht'').2; exact ⟨this.1.le, this.2.le⟩
  have hc0 : c 0 = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hrange ▸ Finset.mem_coe.mpr h0_mem
    exact le_antisymm (hj ▸ c.monotone (Fin.zero_le j)) (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem 0)).1
  have hclast : c (Fin.last (k + 1)) = 1 := by
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hrange ▸ Finset.mem_coe.mpr h1_mem
    exact le_antisymm (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem _)).2 (hj ▸ c.monotone (Fin.le_last j))
  have hno_cross : ∀ (j : Fin (k + 1)) (t : ℚ),
      t ∈ Set.Ioo (c j.castSucc) (c j.succ) → ∀ φ ∈ Φ, φ (γ t) ≠ 0 := by
    intro j t ht φ hφ hzero
    have ht0 : 0 < t := lt_of_le_of_lt (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem j.castSucc)).1 ht.1
    have ht1 : t < 1 := lt_of_lt_of_le ht.2 (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem j.succ)).2
    have hlin : (1 - t) * φ p₁ + t * φ q₁ = 0 := by
      simpa [γ, map_add, map_smul, smul_eq_mul] using hzero
    have hne : φ p₁ ≠ φ q₁ := fun heq => hp₁_out φ hφ (by rw [heq] at hlin; linarith)
    have hteq : t = φ p₁ / (φ p₁ - φ q₁) := by
      have hsub : φ p₁ - φ q₁ ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr hne
      field_simp [hsub]; linarith
    have ht_node : t ∈ nodes := Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem
      (Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_image.mpr
        ⟨φ, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨hφ, hne⟩, hteq.symm⟩, ht0, ht1⟩))
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hrange ▸ Finset.mem_coe.mpr ht_node
    have h1 : (j : ℕ) < (i : ℕ) := c.lt_iff_lt.mp (hi.symm ▸ ht.1)
    have h2 : (i : ℕ) < (j : ℕ) + 1 := c.lt_iff_lt.mp (hi.symm ▸ ht.2)
    omega
  let mid : Fin (k + 1) → ℚ := fun j => (c j.castSucc + c j.succ) / 2
  have hmid_Ioo : ∀ j : Fin (k + 1), mid j ∈ Set.Ioo (c j.castSucc) (c j.succ) := fun j => by
    have hlt : c j.castSucc < c j.succ := c.strictMono Fin.castSucc_lt_succ
    exact ⟨by simp only [mid]; linarith, by simp only [mid]; linarith⟩
  have hmid_C : ∀ j : Fin (k + 1),
      ∃ h ∈ G, permAct h⁻¹ (γ (mid j)) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := fun j => by
    have hm0 : 0 ≤ mid j := le_trans (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem j.castSucc)).1 (hmid_Ioo j).1.le
    have hm1 : mid j ≤ 1 := le_trans (hmid_Ioo j).2.le (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem j.succ)).2
    obtain ⟨h', hh', hh'C⟩ := exists_permAct_mem_maxOrbitCone m G
      (fun i => (hγ_pos (mid j) hm0 hm1 i).le)
    exact ⟨h'⁻¹, G.inv_mem hh', by simpa only [inv_inv] using hh'C⟩
  choose h hhG hhC using hmid_C
  have hendpoints : ∀ j : Fin (k + 1),
      permAct (h j)⁻¹ (γ (c j.castSucc)) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G ∧
      permAct (h j)⁻¹ (γ (c j.succ)) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := fun j => by
    have hpair : ∀ ℓ ∈ F,
        0 ≤ ℓ (permAct (h j)⁻¹ (γ (c j.castSucc))) ∧ 0 ≤ ℓ (permAct (h j)⁻¹ (γ (c j.succ))) := by
      intro ℓ hℓ
      let φ : Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ) := ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv (h j)⁻¹).toLinearMap
      have hφ : φ ∈ Φ := hwall (h j) (hhG j) ℓ hℓ
      have hφ_eval : ∀ t : ℚ, φ (γ t) = (1 - t) * φ p₁ + t * φ q₁ := fun t => by
        simp [γ, map_add, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
      have hfm : 0 < (1 - mid j) * φ p₁ + mid j * φ q₁ := by
        rw [← hφ_eval]
        exact lt_of_le_of_ne ((hC_iff _).mp (hhC j) ℓ hℓ)
          (hno_cross j (mid j) (hmid_Ioo j) φ hφ).symm
      have hres := rational_affine_nonneg_of_no_zero (hmid_Ioo j).1 (hmid_Ioo j).2 hfm
        fun t ht => by rw [← hφ_eval]; exact hno_cross j t ht φ hφ
      have hres1 : 0 ≤ φ (γ (c j.castSucc)) := by rw [hφ_eval]; exact hres.1
      have hres2 : 0 ≤ φ (γ (c j.succ)) := by rw [hφ_eval]; exact hres.2
      exact ⟨hres1, hres2⟩
    exact ⟨(hC_iff _).mpr fun ℓ hℓ => (hpair ℓ hℓ).1, (hC_iff _).mpr fun ℓ hℓ => (hpair ℓ hℓ).2⟩
  have hh0 : h 0 = 1 := by
    have h0C : permAct (h 0)⁻¹ p₁ ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := by
      simpa [γ, hc0] using (hendpoints 0).1
    have hfix := permAct_eq_self_of_mem_maxOrbitCone m G (fun i => (hp₁_pos i).le)
      (G.inv_mem (hhG 0)) hp₁C h0C
    exact inv_eq_one.mp (eq_one_of_permAct_eq_of_notMem_coordEq hfix fun a b hab hmem =>
      hp₁_out _ (heq_mem a b hab) hmem)
  have hhlast : h (Fin.last k) = g := by
    have hlastC : permAct (h (Fin.last k))⁻¹ q₁ ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := by
      simpa [γ, hclast] using (hendpoints (Fin.last k)).2
    have hcompC : permAct ((h (Fin.last k))⁻¹ * g) (permAct g⁻¹ q₁) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := by
      rw [← permAct_mul, mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel, mul_one]; exact hlastC
    have hfix := permAct_eq_self_of_mem_maxOrbitCone m G (x := permAct g⁻¹ q₁)
      (fun i => (hq₁_pos (g⁻¹.symm i)).le)
      (G.mul_mem (G.inv_mem (hhG (Fin.last k))) hg) hq₁_gC hcompC
    rw [← permAct_mul, mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel, mul_one] at hfix
    have hfix' : permAct (g * (h (Fin.last k))⁻¹) q₁ = q₁ := by
      rw [permAct_mul, hfix, ← permAct_mul, mul_inv_cancel, permAct_one]
    exact (mul_inv_eq_one.mp (eq_one_of_permAct_eq_of_notMem_coordEq hfix' fun a b hab hmem =>
      hq₁_out _ (heq_mem a b hab) hmem)).symm
  have hstep : ∀ j : Fin k,
      h j.castSucc * (h j.succ)⁻¹ ∈ Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} := fun j => by
    let t := c j.succ.castSucc
    have ht_eq : c j.castSucc.succ = t := rfl
    have h1C : permAct (h j.castSucc)⁻¹ (γ t) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G :=
      ht_eq ▸ (hendpoints j.castSucc).2
    have h2C : permAct (h j.succ)⁻¹ (γ t) ∈ maxOrbitCone m G := (hendpoints j.succ).1
    have ht_nonneg : ∀ i, 0 ≤ permAct (h j.castSucc)⁻¹ (γ t) i := fun i =>
      (hγ_pos t (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem _)).1 (hc_bounds _ (hc_mem _)).2 _).le
    have hcompC : permAct ((h j.succ)⁻¹ * h j.castSucc) (permAct (h j.castSucc)⁻¹ (γ t)) ∈
        maxOrbitCone m G := by
      rw [← permAct_mul, mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel, mul_one]; exact h2C
    have hfix := permAct_eq_self_of_mem_maxOrbitCone m G ht_nonneg
      (G.mul_mem (G.inv_mem (hhG j.succ)) (hhG j.castSucc)) h1C hcompC
    rw [← permAct_mul, mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel, mul_one] at hfix
    have hfix_step : permAct (h j.castSucc * (h j.succ)⁻¹) (γ t) = γ t := by
      rw [permAct_mul, hfix, ← permAct_mul, mul_inv_cancel, permAct_one]
    rcases eq_one_or_isSwap_of_permAct_eq hfix_step (fun a b c' d' hab hcd h1 h2 =>
      hγ_uniq t (heq_mem a b hab) (heq_mem c' d' hcd) h1 h2) with h1 | hswap
    · rw [h1]; exact one_mem _
    · exact Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨G.mul_mem (hhG j.castSucc) (G.inv_mem (hhG j.succ)), hswap⟩
  have hall : ∀ j : Fin (k + 1), h j ∈ Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} := by
    intro j
    induction j using Fin.induction with
    | zero => rw [hh0]; exact one_mem _
    | succ j ih =>
      have hmul : h j.succ = (h j.castSucc * (h j.succ)⁻¹)⁻¹ * h j.castSucc := by group
      rw [hmul]
      exact Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.inv_mem _ (hstep j)) ih
  rw [← hhlast]
  exact hall (Fin.last k)

/-- **Negative direction of the permutation SAGBI criterion (Reichstein / Thiéry–Thomassé):**
if `m.maxOrbitExponents G` is finitely generated on a finite type `σ`, then `G` is generated by
transpositions. -/
private theorem closure_isSwap_eq_of_fg_maxOrbitExponents [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ]
    (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ))
    (hfg : (m.maxOrbitExponents G).FG) :
    Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} = G := by
  classical
  cases nonempty_fintype σ
  let _ : Fintype G := Fintype.ofFinite G
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF₀⟩ := PointedCone.fg_iff_dualFG.mp (fg_maxOrbitCone m G hfg)
  let F : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)) := F₀.filter (· ≠ 0)
  have hC_iff : ∀ x : σ → ℚ, x ∈ maxOrbitCone m G ↔ ∀ ℓ ∈ F, 0 ≤ ℓ x := fun x => by
    rw [← hF₀, PointedCone.mem_dual]
    exact ⟨fun hx ℓ hℓ => hx (Finset.mem_filter.mp hℓ).1, fun hx ℓ hℓ => by
      rcases eq_or_ne ℓ 0 with rfl | hℓ0
      · simp
      · exact hx ℓ (Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨hℓ, hℓ0⟩)⟩
  let wallFuncs : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)) :=
    (Finset.univ ×ˢ F).image fun p : G × Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ) =>
      p.2.comp (permActLinearEquiv (p.1 : Perm σ)⁻¹).toLinearMap
  let eqFuncs : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)) :=
    ((Finset.univ : Finset (σ × σ)).filter fun p => p.1 ≠ p.2).image fun p =>
      (LinearMap.proj p.1 : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj p.2
  let Φ : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)) := wallFuncs ∪ eqFuncs
  have hwall : ∀ h ∈ G, ∀ ℓ ∈ F, ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv h⁻¹).toLinearMap ∈ Φ := fun h hh ℓ hℓ =>
    Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr
      ⟨(⟨h, hh⟩, ℓ), Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hℓ⟩, rfl⟩)
  have heq_mem : ∀ a b : σ, a ≠ b →
      ((LinearMap.proj a : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj b) ∈ Φ := fun a b hab =>
    Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr
      ⟨(a, b), Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hab⟩, rfl⟩)
  have hΦ_ne_zero : ∀ φ ∈ Φ, φ ≠ 0 := fun φ hφ => by
    rcases Finset.mem_union.mp hφ with hw | he
    · obtain ⟨⟨h, ℓ⟩, hp, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hw
      intro h0
      apply (Finset.mem_filter.mp (Finset.mem_product.mp hp).2).2
      refine LinearMap.ext fun w => ?_
      have hw0 : ℓ (permAct (h : Perm σ)⁻¹ (permAct (h : Perm σ) w)) = 0 :=
        LinearMap.congr_fun h0 (permAct (h : Perm σ) w)
      rw [← permAct_mul, inv_mul_cancel, permAct_one] at hw0
      exact hw0
    · obtain ⟨⟨a, b⟩, hp, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp he
      intro h0
      have := LinearMap.congr_fun h0 (Pi.single a (1 : ℚ))
      simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne (Finset.mem_filter.mp hp).2.symm] at this
  let ℋ : Finset (Submodule ℚ (σ → ℚ)) := Φ.image LinearMap.ker
  have hℋ_ne_top : ∀ H ∈ ℋ, H ≠ ⊤ := fun H hH => by
    obtain ⟨φ, hφ, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hH
    exact fun htop => hΦ_ne_zero φ hφ (LinearMap.ker_eq_top.mp htop)
  have hΦ_perm : ∀ (h : Perm σ), h ∈ G → ∀ φ ∈ Φ,
      LinearMap.ker (φ.comp (permActLinearEquiv h).toLinearMap) ∈ ℋ := fun h hh φ hφ => by
    rcases Finset.mem_union.mp hφ with hw | he
    · obtain ⟨⟨k, ℓ⟩, hp, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hw
      have hcomp : (ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv (k : Perm σ)⁻¹).toLinearMap).comp
          (permActLinearEquiv h).toLinearMap =
          ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv ((h⁻¹ * (k : Perm σ)) : Perm σ)⁻¹).toLinearMap :=
        LinearMap.ext fun w => by
          change ℓ (permAct (k : Perm σ)⁻¹ (permAct h w)) = _
          rw [← permAct_mul, mul_inv_rev, inv_inv]
          rfl
      rw [hcomp]
      exact Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (hwall _ (G.mul_mem (G.inv_mem hh) k.2) ℓ
        (Finset.mem_product.mp hp).2)
    · obtain ⟨⟨a, b⟩, hp, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp he
      have hcomp : ((LinearMap.proj a : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj b).comp
          (permActLinearEquiv h).toLinearMap =
          (LinearMap.proj (h.symm a) : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ) - LinearMap.proj (h.symm b) :=
        LinearMap.ext fun w => rfl
      rw [hcomp]
      exact Finset.mem_image_of_mem _
        (heq_mem (h.symm a) (h.symm b) (h.symm.injective.ne (Finset.mem_filter.mp hp).2))
  obtain ⟨p₀, hp₀_pos, hp₀_out⟩ := exists_perturb_pos_and_notMem
    (fun _ : σ => (1 : ℚ)) (Finset.univ.image fun i : σ => (LinearMap.proj i : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ))
    (fun φ hφ => by obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hφ; exact zero_lt_one)
    ℋ hℋ_ne_top
  obtain ⟨h₀, hh₀G, hp₁C⟩ := exists_permAct_mem_maxOrbitCone m G fun i =>
    (hp₀_pos (LinearMap.proj i) (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ i))).le
  let p₁ : σ → ℚ := permAct h₀ p₀
  have hp₁_pos : ∀ i, 0 < p₁ i := fun i =>
    hp₀_pos (LinearMap.proj (h₀.symm i)) (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ _))
  have hp₁_out : ∀ φ ∈ Φ, φ p₁ ≠ 0 := fun φ hφ h0 =>
    hp₀_out _ (hΦ_perm h₀ hh₀G φ hφ) (by simpa [permActLinearEquiv, p₁] using h0)
  refine le_antisymm ((Subgroup.closure_le G).2 fun _ h => h.1) fun g hg => ?_
  let q₀ : σ → ℚ := permAct g p₁
  let pairSubs : Finset (Submodule ℚ (σ → ℚ)) :=
    ((ℋ ×ˢ ℋ).filter fun P => P.1 ≠ P.2).image fun P => Submodule.span ℚ {p₁} ⊔ (P.1 ⊓ P.2)
  let ℬ : Finset (Submodule ℚ (σ → ℚ)) := ℋ ∪ pairSubs
  have hℬ_ne_top : ∀ K ∈ ℬ, K ≠ ⊤ := fun K hK => by
    rcases Finset.mem_union.mp hK with h1 | h2
    · exact hℋ_ne_top K h1
    · obtain ⟨⟨H₁, H₂⟩, hP, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp h2
      obtain ⟨h12, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.mp hP
      obtain ⟨hH₁, hH₂⟩ := Finset.mem_product.mp h12
      obtain ⟨φ₁, hφ₁, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hH₁
      obtain ⟨φ₂, hφ₂, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hH₂
      exact span_sup_inf_ker_ne_top hne (hp₁_out φ₁ hφ₁) (hp₁_out φ₂ hφ₂)
  let Lpos : Finset (Module.Dual ℚ (σ → ℚ)) :=
    (Finset.univ.image fun i : σ => (LinearMap.proj i : (σ → ℚ) →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ)) ∪
    (F.image fun ℓ => ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv g⁻¹).toLinearMap)
  have hLpos : ∀ φ ∈ Lpos, 0 < φ q₀ := fun φ hφ => by
    rcases Finset.mem_union.mp hφ with h1 | h2
    · obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp h1; exact hp₁_pos (g.symm i)
    · obtain ⟨ℓ, hℓ, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp h2
      have hval : (ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv g⁻¹).toLinearMap) q₀ = ℓ p₁ := by
        change ℓ (permAct g⁻¹ (permAct g p₁)) = ℓ p₁
        rw [← permAct_mul, inv_mul_cancel, permAct_one]
      rw [hval]
      have hne : ℓ p₁ ≠ 0 := by
        have hcomp : ℓ = ℓ.comp (permActLinearEquiv (1 : Perm σ)⁻¹).toLinearMap :=
          LinearMap.ext fun w => by
            change ℓ w = ℓ (permAct (1 : Perm σ)⁻¹ w)
            rw [inv_one, permAct_one]
        rw [hcomp]
        exact hp₁_out _ (hwall 1 G.one_mem ℓ hℓ)
      exact lt_of_le_of_ne ((hC_iff p₁).mp hp₁C ℓ hℓ) hne.symm
  obtain ⟨q₁, hq₁_L, hq₁_ℬ⟩ := exists_perturb_pos_and_notMem q₀ Lpos hLpos ℬ hℬ_ne_top
  refine mem_closure_isSwap_of_generic_segment m G F hC_iff Φ hwall heq_mem hg
    hp₁_pos
    (fun i => hq₁_L _ (Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ i))))
    hp₁C
    ((hC_iff _).mpr fun ℓ hℓ =>
      (hq₁_L _ (Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hℓ))).le)
    hp₁_out
    (fun φ hφ h0 => hq₁_ℬ _ (Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hφ)) h0)
    (fun t {φ₁ φ₂} hφ₁ hφ₂ h1 h2 => by
      by_contra hne
      rcases eq_or_ne t 0 with rfl | ht0
      · exact hp₁_out φ₁ hφ₁ (by simpa using h1)
      · have hdecomp : q₁ = (-(1 - t) / t) • p₁ + t⁻¹ • ((1 - t) • p₁ + t • q₁) := by
          ext i; simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]; field_simp [ht0]; ring
        have hmem : q₁ ∈ Submodule.span ℚ {p₁} ⊔ (LinearMap.ker φ₁ ⊓ LinearMap.ker φ₂) := by
          rw [hdecomp]
          exact Submodule.add_mem_sup (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span rfl))
            ((LinearMap.ker φ₁ ⊓ LinearMap.ker φ₂).smul_mem t⁻¹ ⟨h1, h2⟩)
        exact hq₁_ℬ _ (Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr
          ⟨(LinearMap.ker φ₁, LinearMap.ker φ₂), Finset.mem_filter.mpr
            ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hφ₁, Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hφ₂⟩,
              hne⟩, rfl⟩)) hmem)

end Negative

/-! ### Main equivalence theorems -/

section Main

variable {σ R : Type*}

/-- **Leading-exponent monoid characterization (Reichstein / Thiéry–Thomassé):** for a finite type
`σ`, a permutation subgroup `G ≤ Equiv.Perm σ`, and any monomial order `m`, the monoid
`m.maxOrbitExponents G` of `m`-maximal orbit exponents is finitely generated if and only if `G` is
generated by transpositions. -/
theorem fg_maxOrbitExponents_iff_closure_isSwap_eq [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ]
    (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) :
    (m.maxOrbitExponents G).FG ↔ Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} = G := by
  constructor
  · exact closure_isSwap_eq_of_fg_maxOrbitExponents m G
  · intro hG
    rw [← m.leadingExponents_permInvariantSubalgebra_eq G ℚ]
    exact m.fg_leadingExponents_of_finite_isSAGBIBasis (blockEsymmSet_finite G ℚ)
      (m.isSAGBIBasis_blockEsymmSet G ℚ hG)

/-- **Finite SAGBI criterion for permutation-invariant polynomial algebras (Reichstein /
Thiéry–Thomassé):** over any nontrivial commutative semiring `R` without zero divisors (in
particular, over any field in any characteristic) and for any monomial order `m`, the
`G`-invariant subalgebra `MvPolynomial.permInvariantSubalgebra G R` has a finite `m`-SAGBI basis
if and only if `G` is generated by transpositions. -/
theorem exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff [Finite σ] [DecidableEq σ]
    (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*)
    [CommSemiring R] [NoZeroDivisors R] [Nontrivial R] :
    (∃ B : Set (MvPolynomial σ R), B.Finite ∧
        m.IsSAGBIBasis B (permInvariantSubalgebra G R)) ↔
      Subgroup.closure {τ : Perm σ | τ ∈ G ∧ τ.IsSwap} = G := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨B, hBfin, hB⟩
    have hfg : (m.maxOrbitExponents G).FG := by
      rw [← m.leadingExponents_permInvariantSubalgebra_eq G R]
      exact m.fg_leadingExponents_of_finite_isSAGBIBasis hBfin hB
    exact (m.fg_maxOrbitExponents_iff_closure_isSwap_eq G).mp hfg
  · intro hG
    exact ⟨blockEsymmSet G R, blockEsymmSet_finite G R, m.isSAGBIBasis_blockEsymmSet G R hG⟩

/-- **Product-of-symmetric-groups form of the permutation SAGBI criterion:**
`permInvariantSubalgebra G R` has a finite `m`-SAGBI basis if and only if `G` equals the fiber
subgroup of its orbit quotient map (the product of the full symmetric groups on its orbits). -/
theorem exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff_eq_fiberSubgroup
    [Finite σ] (m : MonomialOrder σ) (G : Subgroup (Perm σ)) (R : Type*)
    [CommSemiring R] [NoZeroDivisors R] [Nontrivial R] :
    (∃ B : Set (MvPolynomial σ R), B.Finite ∧
        m.IsSAGBIBasis B (permInvariantSubalgebra G R)) ↔
      G = TauCeti.fiberSubgroup (Quotient.mk (MulAction.orbitRel G σ)) := by
  classical
  rw [m.exists_finite_isSAGBIBasis_permInvariantSubalgebra_iff G R,
    TauCeti.closure_isSwap_eq_iff_eq_fiberSubgroup_orbitRel G]

end Main

end MonomialOrder
